# Working_Documents — local repository
#
# This file is owned and tracked by the engine repository above this directory. The local
# repository ignores it. See README.md for the ownership split and setup instructions.

# The three files the engine repository owns and ships.
#
# README.md documents the convention; this file and .gitattributes make it work on a fresh
# clone. All three are tracked upstream, so tracking them here as well would put one file
# under two histories with no way to tell which is authoritative. Edit them, and commit them
# from the engine repository.
#
# Everything else in this directory belongs to the local repository. That is the whole
# division: the engine repo owns the scaffolding that defines the convention, the local repo
# owns the documents it holds.
README.md
.gitignore
.gitattributes
